invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma_sign.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_ifma_sign_select
reason: table_select's register loop stops one register short, so the top
  eight lanes of every entry it reads keep what the output held before:
  the product by the entry then multiplies by a number whose high digits
  belong to an earlier step. The rsa_ifma_sign_select proof states that
  every lane of the build's registers holds the digit's entry, for every
  register count the build admits.

--- old
    for (size_t j = 0; j < registers; j++) {
        rsa_ifma_lanes picked = lanes_zero();
--- new
    for (size_t j = 0; j + 1 < registers; j++) {
        rsa_ifma_lanes picked = lanes_zero();
